NAME
    mv - move or rename a file or directory

SYNOPSIS
    mv <src> <dst>

SUSPENDED
    This command currently refuses to do anything. A published build puts
    its own binaries in '/lib/EmuSen', inside this root - see 'man hier' -
    and nothing in this shell tells the install apart from your data, so
    'mv' could quietly relocate the running application out from under
    itself. Parked until the tree distinguishes the two. Everything below
    describes what it does when re-enabled.

DESCRIPTION
    Moves/renames a real file or directory. If <dst> is an existing
    directory, <src> lands inside it ('mv foo.txt logs/' -> 'logs/foo.txt'),
    matching real mv. An existing destination FILE is silently overwritten
    (no -i prompt anywhere in this shell, by design). Both <src> and <dst>
    must resolve inside the project's own directory tree - see 'cd'.

EXAMPLES
    mv scratch.txt home/Logs/
